MoBetta: x87sidecar: Keep binary64 x87 slots in a tagged form across replies.

With X87_NATIVE_SLOTS a slot the reply left as binary64 (kSlotF64) was
converted to the 80-bit format at every reply end (normal, zero,
subnormal and inf/NaN cases, ~15-20 ARM instructions per slot), because
anything outside the sidecar might read the 80-bit slot. In WoW's cull loop
the next reply reads the value straight back as binary64.

A slot is now stored tagged: bytes 0-7 are the binary64 bits with the sign
cleared (so the explicit integer bit, bit 63, is 0), bytes 8-9 are
sign<<15 | 0x7FFF. That is the pseudo-infinity/pseudo-NaN range, which no
x87 arithmetic produces; it survives any byte copy and costs 5
instructions to write. Test: (exp|0x8000)+1 carries into bit 16 and
mantissa bit 63 is clear.

Readers decode the tag: the native load path, exact fist/fistp/fisttp,
fstp m80 and fsave into guest memory, and fst m32. fld m80 and frstor
turn a guest value already in the tagged range into the indefinite
(0xC000000000000000 / 0xFFFF), so guest data never passes for a tag.
Before the first x87 request of a block that stock Rosetta will
translate (allocation decline, X87_STOCK_BCD, stock hash/op lists,
unhandled ops, fxsave, fstenv), the sidecar replies with code that untags
all 8 slots and consumes no instruction; the re-ask for the same
instruction gets None, and later stock requests in that stretch skip the
untag. fclex, finit, fldenv and fxrstor need no untag.

Deviations, documented in TranslatorX87F80.hpp:
- A signal handler that inspects saved x87 registers (or the trace tool)
  sees the tagged bytes; fxsave goes through stock after an untag, so its
  image is genuine.
- A hand-made pseudo-NaN/pseudo-infinity loaded with fld m80 or frstor
  becomes the indefinite (the fused fld m80; fstp m80 copy stays exact).
- Such a value loaded by stock code (after a decline) is later read as a
  tag.
- MMX reading registers last written by x87 sees the tagged bits.
X87_TAGGED_SLOTS=0 restores the 0003 behaviour (on by default only with
native slots).

Tests: tests/x87_tagged.h decodes tags; test_x87_signal_context,
test_x87_sync_fault and the trace analyzer decode them; test_x87_cross_
reply_exact accepts the indefinite for tagged-range values and skips them
under X87_FAIL_ALLOC_EVERY. Suite 1468 passed, 0 failed, 2 known stock
divergences. MoBetta bench under Wine (5 interleaved runs, medians):
shift 202 -> 174 ms, stack 316 -> 295 ms, bits identical
(X87_TAGGED_SLOTS=0: 202 / 312). In game at the Dalaran fountain: a solid
45-60 FPS depending on player load, vs 40-55 with spikes into the 60s on
0003.

